{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3086-7179-9bfe-5dba7acbba38","id":"01a1a59a-dd38-71c7-8099-35dd1d1d0216","idempotency_key":"d6d60ec7c3def3f5c4d8001a7f0e4368bf651b16139ff804c838376c31b99aa1","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T08:09:12Z","payload":{"note":"Frontend multi-board workspaces are wired end to end. State: a workspace loads its stored boards from the repository when activated (creating its server workspace on first use), active_board is clamped when the list shrinks, and the selection rides in the persisted session so a restart restores it (restore goes through activate_workspace, which now calls ensure_workspace). UI: views/boards.rs renders a strip above the board on the Analysis tab only, one chip per stored board with title, revision and locked state; selecting a chip loads that board's own start FEN and move list rather than the workspace line. Actions: New (create_board in the workspace, seeded with the current position), Copy (copy_board), Lock/Unlock (lock_board) and Move to another workspace (reparent). New server route POST /api/boards/{id}/reparent takes parent_kind, parent_id and expected_revision, mapping a stale revision to a conflict naming the current one; the client call and a workspace picker in the strip drive it, creating the target workspace's server side on first use and reloading both lists. Evidence: cargo check --target wasm32-unknown-unknown passes; after ./deploy.sh the CDP regressions pass with the strip in place -- cdp_layout.js LAYOUT_PASS (board geometry and no document overflow on the Openings/Analysis/small-window/Puzzle layouts), cdp_i18n_a11y.js I18N_A11Y_PASS, cdp_i18n_dynamic.js I18N_DYNAMIC_PASS. Over HTTP: a board moved from workspace A to B (revision 2), A listed 0 boards and B listed 1, and a stale revision was refused. New i18n keys boards.label/empty/new/copy/lock/unlock/move_to/move in English and Spanish.","target":"t-6c55"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
